AD  - School of Computer Applications, Dhanalakshmi Srinivasan University, Department of Mca, Tiruchirappalli, India
AB  - Generative AI tools play an important role in software development by helping programmers write and improve code. Existing LLM-based code generation method faced challenges in vague user prompts and inconsistent output quality. The proposed FLAN-LLMatic, a role-aware framework that supports code generation using large language models. The framework uses FLAN-T5 to guide prompt creation and task interpretation and divides the process into four stages such as role definition, demand optimization, code writing, and code review. Each stage assigns specific responsibilities to two language model instances, one acting as a programmer and the other as a reviewer. The intelligent agent improves vague user inputs and creates structured prompts that improve code accuracy and relevance. Evaluation on HumanEval and MBBP datasets shows strong performance in code quality, logical consistency, and security. The proposed FLAN-LLMatic framework helps to generate reliable code from natural language and adapts well to different domains. The proposed FLAN-LLMatic supports faster development and reduces the manual effort, making code generation more efficient and accessible for developers across various fields by achieving 9.7 and 9.8 of code quality score.  © 2025 IEEE.
