AB  - Software engineering is transforming into a new form in this era. With the help of Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI), the software engineering phases such as code generation, refactoring, testing, documentation etc., are being automated. Utilizing models such as GitHub Copilot, Amazon CodeWhisperer, and StarCoder, GenAI solutions augment developer productivity by providing real-time code recommendations, debugging support, and natural language-based “vibe coding.” These tools ease the way software production and decrease the time for development; however, they pose new challenges too. Certain challenges are coding “hallucinations,” security flaws, and the spread of bias. It is important to address the challenges listed previously. This requires continuous and strict validation. Along with that there is the need to have explanations for the automation. This could help the new coders to understand and get along with the AI-generated coding. The advent of full-stack autonomous agents, such as Claude from Anthropic, offers the capability to manage end-to-end development with limited human involvement. As GenAI interfaces with IDEs, CI/CD pipelines, and APIs, it cultivates a collaborative software development environment where human creativity and AI enhancement converge, enhancing efficiency and innovation throughout the software lifecycle. © 2026
