AD  - Hacettepe University, Computer Engineering Dept., Ankara, Turkey
AB  - The integration of large language models (LLMs) like ChatGPT into software engineering workflows has sparked interest in their capacity to assist with programming tasks. While these models are often praised for enhancing productivity and reducing cognitive effort, their limitations, particularly in handling complex logic, remain underexplored. This study investigates the practical effects of ChatGPT support in a structured programming environment by applying an exploratory case study with two embedded scenarios: one with ChatGPT assistance and one without. The same task was attempted under both conditions, allowing for a direct comparison of solution correctness, efficiency, and error resolution. Results show that ChatGPT can help generate accurate code and reduce completion time for moderately complex tasks. At the same time, its effectiveness may vary based on the nature of the error and the complexity of the problem. This case study contributes to the growing body of empirical evidence on how generative AI tools affect software development processes in real-world conditions.  © 2025 IEEE.
