AB  - This chapter offers an in-depth analysis of the transformative impact of Artificial Intelligence (AI) on Software Engineering (SE) through the enhancement of development processes and the automation of repetitive jobs. It outlines the incorporation of AI methodologies, including Machine Learning (ML), Natural Language Processing (NLP), Reinforcement Learning (RL), and Deep Learning (DL), throughout the software development lifecycle phases: requirement analysis, coding, testing, debugging, and deployment. Certain AI tools like GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex and some automated testing frameworks are highlighted in this chapter. The tools are meant to increase the productivity of the developer, assuring highest software quality and decrease in the time-to-market. Case studies from prominent technology companies demonstrate substantial improvements in efficiency and reliability resulting from AI use. Furthermore, this chapter brings out the issues as well as the future directions present in the process of including AI in Software Engineering phases. This boosts the confidence to develop intelligent, scalable and adaptable software systems. This work highlights AI's crucial role in evolving traditional software engineering into a more automated, efficient, and intelligent field. © 2026
