AB  - The emergence of large language models (LLMs) such as OpenAI Codex and GitHub Copilot - has changed much about software development. These computers can respond to natural language input to generate functions, code snippets, and even entire programs. This is all possible owing to natural language. In this research paper, the authors analyze and study the findings of earlier empirical studies to evaluate the accuracy and usefulness of AI-generated code. We look at how well different software tasks, results and developers' productivity are related, in terms of performance and quality of results. Nevertheless, evidence suggests that AI-generated code has many problems, especially related to code quality, maintainability, and security. It signifies that AI generated can help increase productivity and speed up the development process. Still, using the 'human in the loop' approach is very important for risk mitigation and assurance of software correctness.  © 2025 IEEE.
